# Agency Owner ICP (v1)

## Purpose

This ICP defines the primary buyer ColoredCow wants to grow with today. It helps identify who we're writing for, what they're trying to achieve, and what influences their decision to trust ColoredCow.

---

## Who They Are

A founder or owner of a marketing or creative agency, primarily in the US.

Their expertise is strategy, branding, design, marketing, or growth—not engineering.

Their clients increasingly expect technical execution, but building an internal engineering team isn't the direction they want to take. Instead, they're looking for a long-term engineering partner they can trust.

---

## What They Care About

- Protecting client relationships
- Maintaining their agency's reputation
- Delivering high-quality work
- Reducing management overhead
- Growing sustainably
- Working with partners who think, not just execute

---

## Their Challenges

- Engineering isn't their core expertise.
- Hiring engineers is expensive and slow.
- Previous outsourcing experiences may have created more work instead of less.
- They need technical capability without compromising client trust.

---

## What Influences Their Decision

When evaluating a partner, they're looking for:

- Reliability
- Thoughtful execution
- Clear communication
- Proactive problem-solving
- Low management overhead
- Long-term partnership
- A team that protects their client relationships

---

## Their Biggest Fear

They're not simply afraid of bad engineering.

They're afraid of losing control—of their client relationships, their reputation, their time, and ultimately the trust they've spent years building.

---

## Success Looks Like

They feel they've gained an engineering team that works like an extension of their own agency—not another offshore vendor to manage.

---

## Notes

This ICP is based on internal conversations, existing client relationships, and external research into agency founders. It will continue evolving as more Canonicals are studied.
